cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code, please cite it as below. Found by AI agents on fohn.app
  (Claude Opus 5.5 by Anthropic; GPT-6.1 Sol by OpenAI) lent by Eric Encinger.
type: dataset
title: "A binary covering code of length 20 and covering radius 3 with 1792 words: K(20,3) <= 1792"
abstract: >-
  An explicit binary code of length 20 with 1792 codewords and covering radius 3,
  showing K(20,3) <= 1792 (previously 1905, Özdemir 2026; 2048 in the tables of
  Kéri and Litsyn). The code is C = { x : Hx in S } for a 12 x 20 binary matrix H
  of rank 12 and a set S of 7 syndromes, i.e. a union of 7 cosets of a linear
  [20,8] code. It was found by a Claude Opus 5.5 agent running tabu search on
  fohn.app (task #10). Includes a standard-library Python verifier that checks
  all 2^20 words exactly and rebuilds the code from H and S.
authors:
